  "quest": {
    "requirements": "Complete The Real Gift; total Fishing skill 30 or higher (including gear and support bonuses) to begin and make the first turn-in.",
    "items": ["One eligible fish per trade (see the turn-in table)."],
    "titles": ["Cordon Bleu Fisher (Giant Catfish or Ogre Eel)", "Ace Angler (Silver Shark)", "Lu Shang-like Fisher King (Titanictus)"],
    "reward": "Gil for every accepted fish, a chance at an item, and titles for certain fish. Notable items: Brigand's Chart and Pirate's Chart (Bhefhel Marlin), Saber Shoot (Gugrusaurus), and Opal Silk (Lik). See the tables for all rewards and later-era restrictions.",
    "walkthrough": [
      "Complete The Real Gift, then talk to Zaldon in Selbina (H-9) with at least 30 total Fishing skill, including gear and support bonuses.",
      "Trade exactly one eligible fish at a time. The first accepted trade completes the quest, even if no item is found. Further turn-ins are repeatable and do not require 30 Fishing skill after completion.",
      "Every accepted trade pays the listed gil and can award at most one item result. Quantities are shown separately. Fish size does not change the item chance.",
      "Giant Catfish and Ogre Eel award Cordon Bleu Fisher; Silver Shark awards Ace Angler; Titanictus awards Lu Shang-like Fisher King. These titles do not require an item drop.",
      "You can obtain Saber Shoot and Opal Silk before learning Serpent Rumors; that key item is needed to catch Lik and Gugrusaurus yourself and to start Indomitable Spirit.",
      "Holding either chart does not redirect its reward roll to the other chart. Make inventory room and avoid trading for a Rare item you already hold: the fish is consumed before the reward is delivered.",
      "Turnabaligi is not accepted under the ToAU ruleset. Its later-era rewards are Dark Ore (1%), Ice Ore (1.4%), and Water Ore (1.4%), plus 340 gil per accepted trade. The era override requires WotG for this turn-in; blocked fish are kept.",
      "The later-era reference table lists additional fish in the base quest script, not extra eligible ToAU turn-ins. Live-server expansion settings or custom changes may differ."
    ],
